{"name":"Maypole","hex":"#bee8d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Maypole","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A place in England:\nA settlement on St Mary's, Isles of Scilly, off the coast of Cornwall .\nA settlement near the village of Chelsfield, borough of Bromley, Greater London .\nA village in Dartford borough, Kent . \nA settlement in Hoath parish, Canterbury district, Kent ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Maypole"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maypole","blocks":[{"text":"A maypole is a tall wooden pole erected as a part of various European folk festivals, around which a maypole dance often takes place."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Maypole_Sweden.jpg/330px-Maypole_Sweden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maypole","wikidata":"Q76574"},{"title":"Maypole (bakery chain)","blocks":[{"text":"Maypole is a Maltese bakery group and convenience-retail chain headquartered in Qormi. The brand traces its origins to 1900 and has grown from a single bakery to a nationwide network of outlets selling bread, baked goods and grocery items. In August 2025, business media reported the opening of the company's 30th outlet in Valletta."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maypole_(bakery_chain)","wikidata":"Q137112624"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/A_Picture_of_a_Southern_Town-_Life_in_Wartime_Reading%2C_Berkshire%2C_England%2C_UK%2C_1945_D25384.jpg/500px-A_Picture_of_a_Southern_Town-_Life_in_Wartime_Reading%2C_Berkshire%2C_England%2C_UK%2C_1945_D25384.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/A_Picture_of_a_Southern_Town-_Life_in_Wartime_Reading%2C_Berkshire%2C_England%2C_UK%2C_1945_D25384.jpg/500px-A_Picture_of_a_Southern_Town-_Life_in_Wartime_Readi